From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Julian Vetter <julian.vetter@vates.tech>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 10:27:31 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] xen: Fix int-to-pointer assignment in do_xen_bzImage64_load()

info->entry is a void pointer, but do_xen_bzImage64_load() assigns the
unsigned long setup_base to it without a cast. GCC 14 turns
-Wint-conversion into an error by default, which breaks the build.

Signed-off-by: Julian Vetter <julian.vetter@vates.tech>

diff --git a/kexec/arch/x86_64/kexec-bzImage64.c b/kexec/arch/x86_64/kexec-bzImage64.c
index 9c03061b4064..1cf2b3bc51b2 100644
--- a/kexec/arch/x86_64/kexec-bzImage64.c
+++ b/kexec/arch/x86_64/kexec-bzImage64.c
@@ -240,7 +240,7 @@ static int do_xen_bzImage64_load(struct kexec_info *info,
 		info->segment[info->nr_segments-1].is_kernel = true;
 	}
 
-	info->entry = setup_base; // Kernel parameters
+	info->entry = (void *)setup_base; // Kernel parameters
 
 
 	/* Tell the kernel what is going on */
